      "code": "FNCE 7970",
      "department": "FNCE",
      "title": "Taxes and Bus Strategy",
      "description": "The objective of this course is to develop a framework for understanding how taxes affect business decisions. Traditional finance and strategy courses do not consider the role of taxes. Similarly, traditional tax courses often ignore the richness of the decision context in which tax factors operate. The key themes of the framework - all parties, all taxes and all costs - are applied to decision contexts such as investments, compensation, organizational form, regulated industries, financial instruments, tax-sheltered investments, mergers and acquisitions, multinational, and multistate. The ultimate goal is to provide a new approach to thinking about taxes (and all forms of government intervention) that will be valuable even as laws and governments change.\nACCT 7970 may be used as an approved substitute for ACCT 2970.\nAuditors need permission.  Wharton MBA course.  MBA students must request enrollment for this class through Course Match and should not use the \"Add to Cart\" or \"Request Permission\" functions.  There are 10 Undergraduate seats available in each section.  Wharton Undergraduate students interested in this course must place a permission request in PATH to be considered for enrollment. This course follows the MBA calendar, which has different deadlines than the undergraduate calendar: https://mba-inside.wharton.upenn.edu/calendars/\n\nClass starts January 20, 2027",
